.TH DV_DEBUG 1 "2026-08-21" "diffvim 2.0" "diffvim scripts"
.SH NAME
dv_debug \- 
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dv_debug
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fIargs\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
NAME\fR
    dv_debug.sh — Debugging tool for the diffvim pipeline\fR
\fR
SYNOPSIS\fR
    dv_debug.sh [-h|--help]\fR
    dv_debug.sh [--keep] <oldfile> <newfile>\fR
\fR
DESCRIPTION\fR
    Takes an old and new file, runs the full diffvim pipeline (compute →\fR
    postprocess → pace → animator) stage by stage, prints diagnostic\fR
    information to the terminal, AND writes the intermediate output of\fR
    each stage to disk under /tmp/dv_debug/ so you can inspect it with\fR
    any external tool (less, cat -A, diff, wc, etc.).\fR
\fR
    Stage files produced:\fR
      /tmp/dv_debug/raw.txt    — Stage 1 (diffvim-compute-cpp output)\fR
      /tmp/dv_debug/post.txt   — Stage 2 (diffvim-postprocess output)\fR
      /tmp/dv_debug/timed.txt  — Stage 3 (pp_pace output)\fR
      /tmp/dv_debug/snap.txt   — Stage 4 (diffvim-animator-c final buffer)\fR
\fR
    The script then compares the animator's final buffer (snap.txt)\fR
    against the new file and reports either a MATCH or a MISMATCH\fR
    (printing the diff in the latter case).\fR
\fR
OPTIONS\fR
    -h, --help     Show this help message and exit 0.\fR
    --keep         Do not clear /tmp/dv_debug/ before running. Useful\fR
                   when you want to compare stage files across runs.\fR
    <oldfile>      Path to the original/source file (initial buffer).\fR
    <newfile>      Path to the target file the animation should produce.\fR
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show detailed help and exit
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR diffvim (1)
